<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magellan's Cross</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1521</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magellan's Cross is a Christian cross planted by the expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cebu">Cebu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, in April 1521, at the baptism of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-humabon">Rajah Humabon</a> and his people. It stands in a small chapel next to the Basilica of the Santo Niño in Cebu City and is said to enclose remains of the original cross within a later wooden casing. It is a symbol of the arrival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in the Philippines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magellans-cross.jpg" alt="Magellan's Cross" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LMP 2001 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magellan%27s_Cross_2024-07-05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
